Skill slot strategy is an important skill to learn, but it isn't the
first skill
to learn.  Early on, learning to survive to face Medusa is important
so
enhance whatever it takes to get there.  Later on, build a strategy
for
each class on what to enhance when.

For a wizard the 29 slots available can enhance all spell schools to
max, dagger to expert, and still have 2 left over.  For a player able
to
survive early games without enhancing the weapon at hand that suggests
the last two slots might be spent on the crowning gift and one other
artifact.  But less skilled players need the extra capabilty of
enhancing
some classes that are in hand early in the game to survive.  I'm not
against my wizards enhancing staff once to get through the early
levels
even if it means some spell class never gets maxed out in the late
game.
Don't survive the early game and there is not late game.



